WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.310
Welcome to Rawaan.

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.950
Start in Record.

3
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.949
This is where a conversation becomes a note you can review.

4
00:00:09.949 --> 00:00:12.829
Choose Record in-person for session audio.

5
00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:15.469
Already have written notes?

6
00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:17.789
Choose Write a summary.

7
00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:21.149
You do not need to create a client before recording.

8
00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:26.039
Choose the microphone you want to use, then press Check.

9
00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:29.159
Allow microphone access if your browser asks.

10
00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:35.238
You can select an existing client now, or leave the client unassigned and add them after recording.

11
00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:42.799
Make sure everyone is ready and has agreed to the recording.

12
00:00:42.799 --> 00:00:46.399
Press Start recording, and focus on the conversation.

13
00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:49.998
When you are finished, press Stop recording.

14
00:00:49.998 --> 00:00:53.038
Rawaan transcribes the audio after you stop.

15
00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:56.318
Keep the page open while it works.

16
00:00:56.318 --> 00:01:00.878
The recording shown here uses a fictional training conversation.

17
00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:09.599
If you did not select a client earlier, Assign Session opens next.

18
00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:13.999
Choose an existing client, or press Create New and complete their details.

19
00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:16.878
Select the client and press Next.

20
00:01:16.878 --> 00:01:20.718
Rawaan now creates a draft from the transcript.

21
00:01:20.718 --> 00:01:24.558
Creating a client alone does not approve the note.

22
00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:29.719
Check the draft against the original conversation.

23
00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:34.999
Open Transcript to review the words captured, especially names and clinical terms.

24
00:01:34.999 --> 00:01:39.718
Return to Notes and choose Edit note to correct anything that needs changing.

25
00:01:39.718 --> 00:01:45.478
The draft is yours to review; approval should wait until it accurately reflects the session.

26
00:01:50.199 --> 00:01:53.719
When you are satisfied, choose Approve and Save Note.

27
00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:56.919
The approved note becomes part of that client's record.

28
00:01:56.919 --> 00:02:02.598
To return to it, open Clients, choose the client, and open Sessions.

29
00:02:02.598 --> 00:02:04.998
Approved notes are read-only.

30
00:02:04.998 --> 00:02:11.158
That is the complete flow: record, assign, review, and save.
